<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
  Entitlements for the outer Lucidos.app signature ONLY.

  NO DOUBLE HYPHEN ANYWHERE IN THIS COMMENT. codesign hands the file to
  AMFIUnserializeXML, whose XML parser rejects a "- -" pair inside a comment
  (strict XML forbids it) and dies with "syntax error near line 6". plutil
  lints the same file as OK, so the breakage is invisible until a signing run.
  Write flag names without their leading hyphens, or move the prose out of the
  file entirely.

  The release path signs with the hardened runtime, because notarization
  requires it and the hardened runtime denies camera access to a binary that
  does not claim it, whatever Info.plist says. So the composer's Camera item
  needs BOTH halves: NSCameraUsageDescription for the consent prompt's copy
  (Info.plist) and this entitlement for the runtime.

  Deliberately minimal. Lucidos is not sandboxed, so nothing here is a
  container permission; each key is a hardened-runtime capability we actually
  exercise. getUserMedia is video-only, so there is no audio-input key: add one
  only in the change that starts capturing audio.

  It is applied to the outer .app and to nothing else. sign_app_bundle also
  signs ~200 loose Mach-O files (the relocatable Postgres tree, the engine, the
  gateway, the CLI), none of which capture anything, and the bundle carries no
  nested bundles or XPC services for deep signing to propagate to.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
	<key>com.apple.security.device.camera</key>
	<true/>
</dict>
</plist>
